  <name>Click targets (demo)</name>
  <description>Large node marks (48 px rings) beside plain tips, on a schematic tree. In the window as it opens (900 px wide, at most 900 px tall) each ring is taller than the rows are apart, so its click square covers its neighbours&apos; nodes. Hover or click: the hover card and the node menu go to the node NEAREST the pointer -- a click right on a plain tip opens that tip, never the large one around it. The two no_mark tips have a node size of 0 (no mark is drawn) and are still a 9 x 9 px target.</description>
